WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.920
- I would come into church
and preach that God loves me.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.453
That God accepts everybody.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.933
And I didn't believe that for myself.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.983
I was walking around wearing a mask.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.160
I'm Reverend Derek Terry,
pastor Saint Peter's UCC.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.760
And I am a Black gay man minister.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.840
So, for a lot of people, the idea of being

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.840
Black, gay, and Christian
are three intersectionalities

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.343
that cannot come together.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.090
I was 19 when I accepted my call to preach

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.120
in the African Methodist Episcopal Church.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.793
I was the fifth generation
of my family at this church.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:57.430
And its bylaws says you can't
ordain someone who's gay

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:58.420
as a minister.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.350
You can't attend, perform,
or condone gay marriage.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.163
I knew that there was not a place for me.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.800
I didn't want that life.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.840
I didn't want the sneaking, the hiding,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.960
the seediness of not
being able to be accepted

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.853
for who I was, as I was.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.153
I resigned.

00:01:23.923 --> 00:01:25.923
(piano)

00:01:28.056 --> 00:01:30.940
When I resigned, I found
the United Church of Christ.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:34.230
Until today, the idea
that we're looking at

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.413
is that I am good enough.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.960
When I first applied to be
the pastor of the church,

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.322
I was very nervous, and I didn't think that

00:01:43.322 --> 00:01:44.853
they would hire me.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.680
And I said I'm gay, I'm young, I'm Black.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.780
And they said, "Okay."

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.760
It is extremely liberating
to be able to come to church,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.190
to be able to stand before people,

00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:02.190
and to be loved and affirmed
for who I am, as I am.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.860
Without hesitation, without fear,

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.270
and knowing that it
simultaneously empowers others

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.103
to do the same.

